cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Importance Sampling via Girsanov's Theorem: Variance Reduction for Out-of-the-Money Options under Black-Scholes"
abstract: >-
  Monte Carlo pricing of out-of-the-money European calls and cash-or-nothing
  digital calls under Black-Scholes by importance sampling: the samples are
  drawn under a measure that adds a constant drift to the Brownian motion, and
  each of them is weighted by the Girsanov likelihood ratio. A note in LaTeX
  with the derivations, the results and the limits of the method, together
  with a Python package, its tests and a single script that reproduces every
  figure and the table of the note.
authors:
  - family-names: "Cepeda Rocandio"
    given-names: "Roberto"
    affiliation: "University of Oviedo"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-15
repository-code: "https://github.com/indexxxxbraker/girsanov-importance-sampling"
